  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Letterpress printed poem of anonymous author on Hahnemuhle Biblio paper, accordion style binding in a miniature box ("jack-in-a-box-book"), 15 folds, edition of 35 numbered copies. Box made of mulberry paper and Turkish marbled paper. </subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text was letterpress printed from metal types on Hahnemuhle Biblio paper that appears to be thin and somehow delicate, but in the same time is very strong. In order to exemplify the text of "Woman" in the feel of the material, it was important to me that the structure of the paper had a certain liveliness, roughness, and uneveness instead of smooth, fine surface. The artwork connects the first page to the last page, the bubbles flow from stanza to stanza. There is no interruption, the flow is continuously, like the rhythm of the poem. Earthy colors were chosen over bright ones, together with a strong red, since red is a very female color to me." Artist Statement of Intent.</subfield>
  </datafield>
